        "original_id": "c8f62a38-290c-512d-b967-40ceadabe778",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaroslav Kvapil, Antonín Dvořák\n- Places: Chudenice, Prague, Kingdom of Bohemia, Central Europe\n- Works: Rusalka\n- Concepts: Czech literature, opera, monarchy, modern Czech Republic\n\nFacts:\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was born on 25 September 1868 in Chudenice in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia is considered the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\n- Rusalka is an opera described as a lyric fairy tale by Antonín Dvořák.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil died on 10 January 1950 in Prague.",
